Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-06-11
Subject: Key real constants by Pascal payload bytes
License: expat

FPC 3.2.0 shares one float constant pool for all real constant kinds, so the
pool key has to preserve the exact real payload together with the float type
and byte-order flag.  That byte identity is intentional: NaNs and signed zeroes
must not collapse just because arithmetic comparison would consider them equal.

The FPC 3.2.0 compiler sources define bestreal as Extended for i386 and x86_64,
and as Double for arm, aarch64, powerpc and powerpc64.

The translated bootstrap compiler can represent the x86 Extended payload in a
C++ long double object whose storage is wider than the 10-byte Pascal payload.

Hashing a key that contains the translated bestreal object would make the pool
depend on storage padding--which is undefined.

Store only the defined Pascal payload bytes in a packed hash key, while targets
whose bestreal is double keep their full 8-byte payload.

--- a/compiler/ncgcon.pas
+++ b/compiler/ncgcon.pas
@@ -95,8 +95,11 @@ implementation
         between all float types. This requires type and hiloswapped flag to
         be matched along with the value }
       type
+        tbestrealbytes = array[0..sizeof(bestreal)-1] of byte;
-        tfloatkey = record
-          value: bestreal;
+        tfloatkeypayload = array[0..9] of byte;
+        tfloatkey = packed record
+          payload_size: byte;
+          payload: tfloatkeypayload;
           typ: tfloattype;
           swapped: boolean;
         end;
@@ -110,6 +113,29 @@ implementation
          hiloswapped : boolean;
 {$endif ARM}
 
+      function bestreal_payload_size: longint;
+        begin
+          result:=sizeof(bestreal);
+          { The float constant pool key is bytewise so NaNs and signed zeroes
+            keep their exact Pascal payload identity.  Do not include
+            translated-storage padding from x87 Extended values.  In the Linux
+            bootstrap matrix this affects i386 and x86_64; arm, aarch64,
+            powerpc and powerpc64 use double as bestreal and keep the full
+            double payload. }
+          if result>sizeof(double) then
+            result:=10;
+        end;
+
+      procedure copy_bestreal_payload(var key: tfloatkey; const r: bestreal);
+        var
+          i, payload_size: longint;
+        begin
+          payload_size:=bestreal_payload_size;
+          key.payload_size:=byte(payload_size);
+          for i:=0 to payload_size-1 do
+            key.payload[i]:=tbestrealbytes(r)[i];
+        end;
+
       begin
         location_reset_ref(location,LOC_CREFERENCE,def_cgsize(resultdef),const_align(resultdef.alignment),[]);
         lastlabel:=nil;
@@ -120,9 +146,9 @@ implementation
         { const already used ? }
         if not assigned(lab_real) then
           begin
-            { there may be gap between record fields, zero it out }
+            { Zero unused payload bytes before hashing the packed key. }
             fillchar(key,sizeof(key),0);
-            key.value:=value_real;
+            copy_bestreal_payload(key,value_real);
             key.typ:=tfloatdef(resultdef).floattype;
 {$ifdef ARM}
             key.swapped:=hiloswapped;
